EN = {}
EN['pre1'] = """Stage 1 theme (1:33, remastered). All 52 bars of the original move over whole: 145 BPM, G minor, the trumpet theme, the piano chorus and the organ bed untouched note for note; only two new bars of night-cherry intro and two of a receding outro were added. The changes are all about being heard: in section C the source trumpet has just two notes, and the real lead is the piano's sixteenth arpeggio, so it is now promoted to the melody chair and carries the whole section; the drums sit within 2 dB of the lead with off-beat kicks and ghost snares so the walk feels like a night path; the low end gains an eighth-note pedal, lifting 63-125 Hz from -12 to -11 dB. At the end it turns back to the top and she walks one more lap.
- Rumia: "Not light yet, right? Then I'll walk one more lap." """
EN['pre2'] = """Stage 2 theme (1:51, remastered). All 48 transcribed bars move over: 151 BPM, C# minor, the three-voice piano of section B kept as written, and the turn to G# minor in its second half untouched. This pass thickens the mist: harpsichord, strings and piano each come up a step (they sat seven to nine dB under the lead), and every bar lays an open-fifth pad and a choir bed under the original bass. Fireflies are dotted in the high register by the music box, the insect chorus is carried by sixteenth-note bass, and the seam still has no outro: it turns back the moment it reaches the end, where she stands holding her lantern.
- Wriggle Nightbug: "Don't rush off. The fireflies haven't gone out yet." """
EN['pre3'] = """Stage 3 theme (1:34, remastered). All 52 bars move over: 143 BPM, E major, the flute melody with its tremolo-string unison kept exactly as written, and the shift to B-flat/D minor in section C untouched. Two things get fixed here: the flute is lifted above the drums (it sat five dB under), and the coda is two beats shorter so the loop point no longer pops. Ice crystals are dotted by thirty-second music-box notes up high, the pendulum tick runs through section A, and piano and harpsichord each come up a step to fill the middle.
- Cirno: "Cold air first, person after. That's the proper order." """
EN['pre4'] = """Stage 4 theme (2:04, remastered). The original runs 152 bars but only 40 of them actually loop (45-84 and 85-124 are note-for-note identical), so this version takes A1-C2 plus the closing D section, 84 bars: 163 BPM, B minor, the three-layer Calliope riff, sixteenth bass and arpeggios untouched. The work is in keeping it un-muddy: flute and second flute used to pile into a six-dB spike and are now levelled with the drums, the bass gains a sub-octave, the kit is rebuilt around the source's taiko and toms; two bars of water drops open it and two bars of pool close it. The mountain wind has not changed breath in seventy days, and that much is true.
- Aya Shameimaru: "The waterfall won't stop and neither will I. One shot, then I'm gone." """
EN['pre6'] = """Stage 6 theme (1:23, remastered). All 58 bars move over, including the sixteen bars of 3/4 in the middle: 162 BPM, D minor, the piano's left-hand sixteenth toccata and right-hand top line untouched, and the turn to B major / D# minor in section C kept as written. The source has no separate bass track, so an eighth-note pedal and a sub are added from each bar's lowest note; the top line reaches D#8, so the whole lead is folded back an octave on rebuild rather than piercing an eardrum; two bars of take-off before and two of landing after park the train at the gate of Eientei.
- Kaguya Houraisan: "I have ridden this train. Don't ask me the time before we arrive." """

